WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.546
The microscope began as a purchase near Qasr El Einy in

00:00:04.546 --> 00:00:07.897
Cairo. Bringing it back to Qatar was harder than

00:00:07.897 --> 00:00:09.014
carrying a box.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:21.830
I purchased a microscope near Qasr El Einy in Cairo. It

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.414
was not laboratory equipment assigned to me by a

00:00:25.414 --> 00:00:25.812
university.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.629
Bringing it with me to Qatar was a considerable hassle.

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:40.127
The difficulty did not end when I had paid for it.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:51.991
With a microscope at home, observation no longer

00:00:51.991 --> 00:00:55.531
depended entirely on laboratory booking hours or a

00:00:55.531 --> 00:00:56.417
scheduled class.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.755
The instrument let me pursue small independent

00:01:05.755 --> 00:01:09.060
observations simply because I wanted to understand

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:09.532
something.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.522
There were things I wanted to inspect without waiting

00:01:20.522 --> 00:01:24.142
for a university timetable. The instrument made those

00:01:24.142 --> 00:01:25.047
investigations possible.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:34.794
Ownership did not confer a scientific result; it made

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:38.172
curiosity more practical by providing repeated access.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.738
The value of owning a microscope was not prestige. It

00:01:47.738 --> 00:01:51.683
was the freedom to return to a question when I had the

00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:52.011
time.
